  "summary": "The G.G. Shinobi is Sega's ninja platform adventure, first released for Game Gear in Japan on 26 April 1991.",
  "body": [
    "The G.G. Shinobi is Sega's ninja platform adventure, first released for Game Gear in Japan on 26 April 1991. Joe Musashi enters Neo City to rescue four captured comrades and stop the power threatening Ninja Valley. Each rescued ninja becomes playable, bringing a different weapon, movement ability and magical technique into the group. The portable game therefore gives the familiar sword-fighting journey a growing cast with practical uses. Progress means recovering the people whose skills will eventually allow the whole team to cross the enemy's most dangerous rooms.",
    "The first four stages can be attempted in any order. Choosing which comrade to rescue first determines which additional abilities become available for the remaining locations. Each character's different equipment and movement changes the immediate approach to enemies and obstacles. Joe begins the mission alone, but successful rescues turn the campaign into a collection of possible responses. A route that is awkward with one ninja can become more manageable with another, giving the player a reason to think about the sequence of stages as well as the action within them.",
    "After the four rescues, Neo City becomes a network of trap rooms that require particular ninjas to cross. Many rooms offer two exits into further challenges, testing the combined abilities gathered during the earlier missions. The final area makes the rescue structure pay off directly: each companion is needed because of what that character can do. Yuzo Koshiro composed the soundtrack. The small handheld adventure gains its scale from the team, with five distinct skill sets turning a compact selection of stages into a connected problem of route, ability and timing."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "Joe Musashi needs his allies",
    "Choosing the first rescue",
    "Five ninjas for the final fortress"
  ],
